      "title": "READ ME: how to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "SCRIPT → 65 PHOTOREAL IMAGES IN ONE CLICK (Runware only)\n\nFIRST TIME ONLY\n1. If a 'missing nodes' box appears: Search → Install (Runware),\n   restart ComfyUI, drag this file in again.\n2. Settings (gear, bottom left) → search 'Runware' →\n   paste your key in 'Runware API key'.\n\nEVERY VIDEO\n1. Paste your script in the green 'PASTE SCRIPT HERE' box.\n2. Change FOLDER NAME to a new name for each video (e.g. video_02).\n3. Leave the Run count at 1 and press Run ONCE.\n   Claude plans all 65 scenes, then all 65 images are made.\n   This takes a while; the 'Loop' box shows 'Iteration x / 65'.\n\nALL IMAGES AT ONCE: ComfyUI's output folder → your FOLDER NAME\n(scene_00001_.png ... scene_00065_.png). Select all → copy.\n\nTest first: set NUMBER OF IMAGES to 5, Run, check the images,\nthen set it back to 65. If a run stops with an error, images are\nnot saved and a new Run makes all of them again.\nOnly change the green boxes. Grey boxes are automatic."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "SCRIPT → 65 PHOTOREAL IMAGES IN ONE CLICK (Runware only)\n\nFIRST TIME ONLY\n1. If a 'missing nodes' box appears: Search → Install (Runware),\n   restart ComfyUI, drag this file in again.\n2. Settings (gear, bottom left) → search 'Runware' →\n   paste your key in 'Runware API key'.\n\nEVERY VIDEO\n1. Paste your script in the green 'PASTE SCRIPT HERE' box.\n2. Change FOLDER NAME to a new name for each video (e.g. video_02).\n3. Leave the Run count at 1 and press Run ONCE.\n   Claude plans all 65 scenes, then all 65 images are made.\n   This takes a while; the 'Loop' box shows 'Iteration x / 65'.\n\nALL IMAGES AT ONCE: ComfyUI's output folder → your FOLDER NAME\n(scene_00001_.png ... scene_00065_.png). Select all → copy.\n\nTest first: set NUMBER OF IMAGES to 5, Run, check the images,\nthen set it back to 65. If a run stops with an error, images are\nnot saved and a new Run makes all of them again.\nOnly change the green boxes. Grey boxes are automatic."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
